>> title: Poke Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: tuna, sushi rice, raw fish, hawaiian, stovetop, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: poke bowl, poke, ahi poke, hawaiian poke bowl, tuna poke bowl, tuna rice bowl, raw fish bowl, rice bowl
>> pairs-with: goma-dare, shichimi-togarashi
>> servings: 4
>> time: 55 min
>> slack: unforgiving — cubed tuna left in soy much past half an hour cures at the edges and turns opaque and firm, and it does not come back
>> step.1: Sushi rice is seasoned hot and fanned cool. Cut the vinegar through rather than stirring it or the grains go to paste.
>> step.2: steam 15 min, rest 10 min
>> step.3: cut the vinegar through, fan it cool
>> step.4: dress, then chill 20 min
>> step.5: macerate 15 min, squeeze dry
>> step.6: build it, fish on one side

Sushi rice is seasoned while it is hot and fanned while it cools.

Steam @sushi rice{1 1/2%cups}(300 g; washed until the water runs clear) with @water{1 3/4%cups}(415 mL) in a covered #saucepan{} ~steam{15%min}, then ~rest{10%min} off the heat.

Fold @rice vinegar{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @granulated sugar{1%Tbs} and @kosher salt{1%tsp} through @&(~1)hot rice{} with a cutting motion, fanning as you go, until it cools to body temperature and shines.

Toss @sushi-grade tuna{1%lb}(450 g; in 3/4-inch cubes) with @soy sauce{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp}(10 mL) and @scallions{2}(sliced), then ~chill{20%min}.

Toss @cucumber{1}(sliced thin) with @rice vinegar{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @kosher salt{1/4%tsp}, leave it to ~macerate{15%min}, then squeeze it dry.

Spread @&(~3)seasoned rice{} across four bowls, spoon @&(~2)marinated tuna{} over one side and @&(~1)cucumber{} over the other, and finish with @avocado{1}(sliced), @nori{1%sheet}(cut into strips) and @toasted sesame seeds{2%tsp}.
